WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.520
SPEAKER: This section gives
you an introduction to Cloud.

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:05.400
Cloud computing enables you to
consume server infrastructure

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:08.483
and software platforms as a
service over the internet.

00:00:08.483 --> 00:00:09.900
You don't have to
buy and maintain

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:12.620
expensive hardware
in your data center.

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:14.450
Infrastructure
includes raw resources

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:18.440
such as virtual machines,
networking, storage, and more.

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:20.600
These resources are the
fundamental building blocks

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:22.550
of cloud computing.

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:26.150
When you consume infrastructure
as a service, IaaS,

00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:28.640
you have greater control
over the resources, but also

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:30.350
greater management overhead.

00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:33.150
For example, consider
a virtual machine.

00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:35.240
You need to install,
upgrade, and patch

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:38.032
all the software required
to run your application.

00:00:38.032 --> 00:00:39.740
You could configure
your virtual machines

00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:42.650
to scale based on the
load on your application.

00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:45.680
Google Compute Engine,
networking, and load balancers

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:47.980
are examples of IaaS.

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:50.740
Platform as a service,
PaaS, provides a platform

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:53.530
with managed services where
runtime environment and network

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:55.360
settings are pre-configured.

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:57.610
This makes it easier for
you to develop and deploy

00:00:57.610 --> 00:00:59.540
your application.

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:03.020
Google App Engine is an example
of platform as a service.

00:01:03.020 --> 00:01:05.540
Google App Engine comes
pre-configured with runtimes

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:09.170
for Java, Python,
Node, and more.

00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:12.680
Software upgrades and patches
are automatically applied.

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:15.440
Load balancing is
also reconfigured.

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:18.380
This enables the developer to
focus on the application logic

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:21.830
only instead of worrying
about infrastructure setup.

00:01:21.830 --> 00:01:24.050
With software as
a service, SaaS,

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:25.940
entire applications
are managed and made

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:27.890
available in the
cloud environment

00:01:27.890 --> 00:01:31.620
Gmail as an example of
a software as a service.

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:33.540
This slide shows how
you can use Google Cloud

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:36.090
Platform for application
data, application

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:39.730
logic, and integration
with other Google services.

00:01:39.730 --> 00:01:43.280
Imagine an online shopping
website or a mobile app.

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:45.220
The application needs
to store and retrieve

00:01:45.220 --> 00:01:47.980
different types of
data as follows.

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:50.380
The website or app
displays images of items

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:52.720
such as shoes and clothes.

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:56.220
These images can be stored
in Google Cloud Storage.

00:01:56.220 --> 00:01:59.190
High volume, semi-structured
data like gaming or streaming

00:01:59.190 --> 00:02:02.400
data can be stored in NoSQL
databases such as Cloud

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:05.060
Datastore and Bigtable.

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:06.620
Customer information
can be stored

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:11.490
in a relational database, such
as Cloud SQL or Cloud Spanner.

00:02:11.490 --> 00:02:13.920
Application logic can
be deployed and executed

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:17.910
on Google App Engine or
Google Kubernetes engine.

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:20.410
You can integrate with other
Google services, such as Google

00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:23.007
Maps and YouTube.

00:02:23.007 --> 00:02:24.840
All of this infrastructure
can be started up

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:27.540
in just a few minutes without
buying hardware or installing

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:29.090
software.

